From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Offload <offload@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 05:29:14 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(plugin-ecommerce): validate variant items before a
 payment starts

A customer can pay one product's price for another. The cart's subtotal
uses the price of each item's variant, and initiate never checks variant
items: the variant branch sits inside the branch for items without a
variant, so it can't run. A guest cart that pairs an expensive product with
a cheap variant of another product, or that buys a product with variants
enabled at the product's own price, reaches the payment adapter and is
charged that subtotal. Variant stock and missing variant prices go unchecked
too.

Initiate now loads each item's product and, when the item has a variant, the
variant. It refuses a variant that belongs to another product and a product
with variants enabled that has no variant, then runs the products validation
with both, which checks the variant's price and stock.

Initiate also refuses:
- a cart that has already been bought, which a second payment would charge
  again;
- a quantity that isn't a whole number of at least 1, which would decrement
  stock by a fraction;
- a product or variant that has never been published, which a guest could
  otherwise buy by its ID;
- a cart whose subtotal no longer matches the current prices. The carts
  collection computes the subtotal only when the cart is saved, so a price
  change left it stale and the customer paid the old price. Initiate saves
  the items again, which recomputes the subtotal, and answers 409 so the
  customer reviews the new total.

Offload-Patch: ecommerce-initiate-variant-validation
Drop-When: the pinned release validates variant items in the initiate endpoint and checks that each variant belongs to its item's product
Tests: pnpm exec vitest run --project unit packages/plugin-ecommerce/src/endpoints/initiatePayment.spec.ts; e2e suite (tests/checkout.spec.ts, the tests that refuse a tampered variant cart)
